WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.272
Su Shi, a great writer of the Northern Song, styled himself the Lay Buddhist Dongpo — he was a man both clever and fun.

00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:10.790
Poetry or essays — he was good at everything.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.748
When he served as an official in Hangzhou, he managed West Lake and dredged its waters.

00:00:16.098 --> 00:00:21.834
The people pitched in together, and the lake's surface slowly grew clear.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:26.792
He also loved to cook, and the braised pork he made was especially delicious.

00:00:27.142 --> 00:00:31.966
He simmered it slowly, and the aroma of the meat filled the kitchen.

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:37.620
Later generations called this braised pork 'Dongpo Pork', and people still eat it today.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.794
Soft, fragrant and sweet, Dongpo Pork is loved by everyone.

00:00:43.144 --> 00:00:47.420
He was exiled several times in his life, yet he always stayed optimistic and open-hearted.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.322
Wherever he went, he faced life with a smile.

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:58.464
Su Dongpo's stories hold both history and legend, and they have warmed generations of readers.

00:00:58.814 --> 00:01:02.678
His optimism and talent have stayed in people's hearts ever since.

